WEBVTT

1
00:00.500 --> 00:05.000
Tonight we read the night sky, one landmark at a time.

2
00:05.000 --> 00:10.500
Watch long enough and every star turns slowly around one point: the north celestial pole.

3
00:10.500 --> 00:16.000
Seven bright stars draw the Great Dipper: four for the bowl, three for the handle.

4
00:16.000 --> 00:21.500
Follow its two pointer stars, Merak then Dubhe, about five times the gap between them…

5
00:21.500 --> 00:26.000
…and you reach Polaris, the pole star, which barely moves all night.

6
00:26.000 --> 00:30.500
On the other side of Polaris, the W of Cassiopeia keeps watch.

7
00:30.500 --> 00:34.000
Find the pointers, follow them north, and you will never lose your way.
